	Someone was commenting re: (see subject line), & managed to imply
that the turn of phrase has something to do with flatulence.

	In point of fact, in medievel times a petard was a demolitions charge
used by combet engineers to attempt to destry a door or barricade of some sort.
If he was incompetent & set the fuse to short or shoved the lighted punk into
the powder itself, he was "hoist by his own petard."

	So call me the evangel of etymology.

